  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows sustained positivity (≥0.5) and model overestimates prices.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if recent true outcomes show mean reversion after sharp spikes.",
    "Increase forecast lag by 1-2 days if sentiment history indicates market uncertainty (0.00-0.33) and model is overly aggressive.",
    "Apply upward bias correction if true outcomes consistently exceed model forecasts during low sentiment periods (0.00-0.33).",
    "Cap forecast growth after 3 consecutive days of upward momentum to prevent overshoot.",
    "Use sentiment history to weight forecast adjustments: higher sentiment → lower adjustment magnitude; lower sentiment → higher adjustment magnitude."
  ]
}
